 "bloques": [
  {
   "tipo": "explicacion",
   "titulo": "Greeting and saying goodbye",
   "texto": [
    "**Здравствуйте** is the formal greeting and is worth any time. Among friends it's called **привет**.",
    "According to the time: **доброе утро** (good morning, morning), **добрый день** (good morning, good evening) and **добрый вечер** (good evening, good night).",
    "To say goodbye: **до свидания** (goodbye) and, among friends, **пока**."
   ]
  },
  {
   "tipo": "explicacion",
   "titulo": "You and you.",
   "texto": [
    "**Ты** is «You» and is usually used with friends, family and children. **Вы** can mean «You» or «You.». With an adult you don't know, **вы** is a prudent option to start with; the relationship, environment and preference of the person also count."
   ]
  },
  {
   "tipo": "explicacion",
   "titulo": "What's your name?",
   "texto": [
    "In Russian it says «They call me»: **Меня зовут Анна** = my name is Anna.",
    "To ask: **Как вас зовут?** (from you) or **Как тебя зовут?** (from you).",
    "You can also say only **Я Антон** (I am Anton): remember that «be» is not said.",
    "When you meet someone: **очень приятно** («very nice»), which is our «Enchanted.».",
    "**А** serves to return the question: **А вы?** (and you?), **А ты?** (and you?)."
   ]
  },
